<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lillebonne</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Juliobona</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lillebonne is a town in Normandy, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pays-de-caux">Pays de Caux</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> estuary. As Juliobona it was the chief town of the Caleti under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, and its Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> is among the best preserved in northern France. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a> held a council of his barons at its castle in 1066 to prepare the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lillebonne.jpg" alt="Lillebonne" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Direction de la communication de Caux Seine agglo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Face_avant_mus%C3%A9e_Juliobona.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
